hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"154","Innā lillāhi wa innā ilayhi rāji'ūn, Allāhumma'jurnī fī muṣībatī, wa'khlif lī khayran minhā.. Indeed, to Allah we belong and to Him we will return. O Allah, reward me in my affliction and replace it with something better."
"155","Allāhumma’ghfir li (name of the person) warfa` darajatahu fi ‘l-mahdiyyīn, wakhlufhu fī `aqibihi fi ‘l-ghābirīn, wagh’fir-lanā wa lahu yā Rabba ‘l-`ālamīn, wafsaḥ lahu fī qabrihi wa nawwir lahu fīh. O Allah, forgive [name of the person] and elevate his station among those who are guided. Send him along the path of those who came before, and forgive us and him, O Lord of the worlds. Enlarge for him his grave, and shed light upon him in it. Reference: Muslim 2/634."
